{
  "_id": "6b05168635d1c7861e96d23c",
  "Package": "OmniCorr",
  "Title": "Multi-Omics Integration and Visualization Framework",
  "Version": "1.1.0",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\n\"Shashank\", \"Gupta\",\nemail = \"bioinformaticssrm2011@gmail.com\",\nrole = \"aut\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0001-8839-7003\")\n),\nperson(\n\"Veronica\", \"Quarato\",\nemail = \"vequa7472@nmbu.no\",\nrole = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"),\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0009-0008-4049-9746\")\n),\nperson(\n\"Wanxin\", \"Lai\",\nrole = \"aut\"\n),\nperson(\ngiven = \"Research Council of Norway\",\nrole = \"fnd\",\ncomment = \"Project 300846\"\n),\nperson(\ngiven = \"European Union\",\nrole = \"fnd\",\ncomment = \"Horizon 2020 ERA-Net Cofund BlueBio (311913); MSCA DN HoloGen (101169005)\"\n),\nperson(\ngiven = \"Novo Nordisk Foundation\",\nrole = \"fnd\",\ncomment = \"Project 0054575-SuPAcow\"\n)\n)",
  "Description": "Provides tools for correlation-based integration and\nvisualization of multi-omics datasets, including\ntranscriptomics, metatranscriptomics, metagenomics,\nmetaproteomics, and associated sample metadata. The package\ncomputes pairwise correlations between independently processed\nomics layers and provides flexible tools for organizing and\nvisualizing cross-omics associations using aligned heatmaps and\noptional network-style visualizations. OmniCorr is designed to\ncomplement existing preprocessing and network inference\nworkflows rather than replace them.",
